  "goodToKnow": "Das Finanzamt is the local tax office. Every German taxpayer deals with it: you submit your Steuererklärung (tax return), usually online through the ELSTER portal, and receive a Steuerbescheid (tax assessment) by post. The self-employed get a Steuernummer from it. A letter vom Finanzamt is famously not what anyone wants in their mailbox. Note the plural with an umlaut: die Finanzämter."
